<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea intervens again, sells dlr-dealers.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea intervens again, sells dlr-dealers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Korea intervened in the interbank market in late afternoon session for the second time on Monday, selling dollars as the won hit the 856.00 won to the U.S. unit, dealers said.</p>
<p>The central bank denied intervening, as it routinely does.</p>
</text>
